inkedin.com%2Fposts%2Felena-gonci_design-is-not-how-it-looks-but-how-it-works-activity-7267222963588902912-cbqf&trk=public_post_comment-cta)\n\n Share \n    *   Copy\n    *   LinkedIn\n    *   Facebook\n    *   Twitter\n\nTo view or add a comment, [sign in](https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Fposts%2Felena-gonci_design-is-not-how-it-looks-but-how-it-works-activity-7267222963588902912-cbqf&trk=public_post_feed-cta-banner-cta)\n\n*   \n[](https://www.linkedin.com/posts/bhavya-t-67a630121_productdesign-ai-uxdesign-activity-7259865145873518592-u2rp)\n\n[![Image 30: View profile for Bhavya T.](https://www.linkedin.com/posts/felixleezd_steve-jobs-on-how-to-perfect-product-design-activity-7259573425705254912-hYCh)](https://ca.linkedin.com/in/bhavya-t-67a630121?trk=public_post_feed-actor-image)[Bhavya T.](https://ca.linkedin.com/in/bhavya-t-67a630121?trk=public_post_feed-actor-name) \nProduct Designer | Specialized in Fintech, SaaS, AI-Web Applications B2B, B2B2C | 0→1 & 1→2 Scalable Products\n\n 7mo    \n\n    *   [Report this post](https://www.linkedin.com/uas/login?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Fposts%2Fbhavya-t-67a630121_productdesign-ai-uxdesign-activity-7259865145873518592-u2rp&trk=public_post_ellipsis-menu-semaphore-sign-in-redirect&guestReportContentType=POST&_f=guest-reporting)\n\nSteve Jobs’ philosophies have always inspired me. They were groundbreaking for a time when digital products were new, a tool to give users control. But here we are in 2025, where AI has become part of that control, and we need to rethink a few things. 🌐 In the 90s and early 2000s, control was clear-cut. Users directed their experience, and products simply responded. But with AI, control is now shared, more complex, and sometimes unpredictable. So when Jobs said, ‘If users need a manual, the design has failed,’ I believe in 2025, design now requires mindful guidance. Not just any guidance, but guidance that respects user autonomy and ethical boundaries. It’s no longer about just making things easy — it’s about making them meaningful. Jobs once emphasized not relying on market research and focusing on the future. I see it differently today. Yes, we still need to show people the future, but market research isn’t an enemy. It’s a way to understand real-world impact, to create a future that’s not just innovative but also responsible and relevant. And ‘Design is not just about how it looks but how it works.’ Now, I’d add, it’s also about what kind of human interactions and habits it nurtures. Are we creating designs that empower users long-term, or are we risking dependency and passive engagement? In this evolved era, product design isn’t just about simplicity or control. It’s about understanding the broader impact of what we create and who we’re creating it for. Let’s make sure our principles evolve, so we’re designing with people, not just for them. 🙌 [#productdesign](https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fproductdesign&trk=public_post-text)[#AI](https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fai&trk=public_post-text)[#uxdesign](https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fuxdesign&trk=public_post-text)[#AIdesign](https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Faidesign&trk=public_post-text)[#uidesign](https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fuidesign&trk=public_post-text)[#productdesigner](https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fproductdesigner&trk=public_post-text)\n\n[![Image 31: View profile for Felix Lee](https://www.linkedin.com/posts/felixleezd_steve-jobs-on-how-to-perfect-product-design